# ============================================================================
# 🚫 Go2My.Link — .gitignore
# ============================================================================
# Tailored for PHP/MySQL development on macOS, Windows & Linux (incl. Debian/Raspberry Pi)
# IDE: Visual Studio Code (with FTP Sync extension) & Xcode
# Hosting: Dreamhost Shared Hosting
#
# This file is dynamically maintained as the project evolves.
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# 🔐 Sensitive Credentials & Secrets
# ============================================================================
# Auth credentials files contain database passwords, encryption keys,
# and third-party API secrets. These MUST NEVER be committed.
# Template files (auth_creds.example.php) ARE tracked for reference.
# ============================================================================
**/auth_creds.php
!**/auth_creds.example.php

# Legacy MWlink config holds a plaintext DB credential — never commit it, and
# never commit the legacy web root it lives in (it must not ship). See #93.
**/dbConfig.php
**/public_html_legacy/

# Installer runtime artefacts (server-local; never commit)
# The shared server-wide credentials dir stays "_auth_keys/"; each
# component's own credential-override dir was renamed from "_auth_keys/" to
# ".auth/". Both patterns are kept so a lock/token file is ignored regardless
# of which directory it ends up in.
**/_auth_keys/.install_token
**/_auth_keys/.installed
**/.auth/.install_token
**/.auth/.installed

# dev-team autopilot loop lock (runtime only — never committed).
.dev-team/loop.lock/

# The dev-team plugin's own notes files (issue #249, owner decision 19, #243).
#
# The plugin writes four of the files it produces as it works — PROJECT.md,
# FEATURES.md and SECURITY.md at the repository ROOT, plus
# .dev-team/autopilot.json — at these fixed paths regardless of which skill is
# running; a skill that writes one of these files writes it at its original
# path (it also writes others, such as VERIFICATION.md or MIGRATION.md, which
# are not covered here — see .claude/memory/working-rules.md, rule 5, for how
# those other files are handled). The copies it wrote during its June–July
# 2026 run were tracked in git and held useful history, so instead of just
# ignoring them, that decision was to KEEP them: they were
# moved with `git mv` to docs/dev-team/, where they still are, still tracked,
# with a README explaining what they are. The root HANDOFF.md below is a
# similar case, not a different one: it held the project's real handoff from
# 2026-07-09 to 2026-09-21 — 36 commits, `git log -- HANDOFF.md` proves it —
# and that content was kept the same way — by moving the file, first to
# .claude/HANDOFF.md and then to .github/HANDOFF.md — rather than by dropping
# it. (That is a minority of the repository's life, not most of it: the
# repository's first commit was 2026-02-22, and the history behind this
# branch runs to 221 commits — not "this branch alone", which would mean
# only the commits unique to it; the earlier wording here overstated it,
# corrected again 2026-09-22.)
# Only the root PATH is scratch-only now, because the plugin keeps writing
# a throwaway card there; the history that used to live at that path was never
# lost, it just moved house.
#
# A run that writes one of these four files still writes it at its ORIGINAL
# path — that habit is unchanged — so all four paths are ignored here. Not
# every run writes all four: only the autopilot loop writes autopilot.json
# (and the plugin's `/dev-team-approve` command, which edits that same file's
# gate ledger rather than writing a fresh one), only featurefind writes
# FEATURES.md, and so on — see the comment above and docs/dev-team/README.md.
# On the first three, the leading slash means "only the file at
# the repository root": docs/dev-team/PROJECT.md, docs/dev-team/FEATURES.md
# and docs/dev-team/SECURITY.md are NOT ignored. .dev-team/autopilot.json
# needs no leading slash for the same reason a leading slash works on the
# other three: a gitignore pattern with a slash anywhere in the middle (not
# just at the start) is already anchored to the directory the .gitignore file
# itself sits in — the repository root here — rather than matching at any
# depth. (Checked: `git check-ignore --no-index web/.dev-team/autopilot.json`
# exits 1 — a copy inside a subfolder is NOT caught by this line.)
# docs/dev-team/autopilot.json is a different path entirely and is NOT
# ignored.
/PROJECT.md
/FEATURES.md
/SECURITY.md
.dev-team/autopilot.json

# The dev-team plugin writes (and tries to commit) its own ~40-line "resume card" at
# HANDOFF.md in the repository ROOT, replacing whatever is there. The project's real
# handoff lives at .github/HANDOFF.md (moved there on 2026-09-22, as the owner asked —
# it was at .claude/HANDOFF.md briefly before that), so the root file is only the
# plugin's scratch copy and must never be committed — otherwise it becomes a second,
# competing handoff (issue #202). The leading slash means "only the root one":
# .github/HANDOFF.md is NOT ignored.
/HANDOFF.md

# MaxMind GeoLite2 database (#43) — a large, licensed, frequently-updated
# binary. NEVER committed; fetched at DEPLOY time by scripts/fetch-geoip.sh
# (see .github/workflows/sftp-deploy.yml). The vendored PURE-PHP READER
# library that reads this file (web/_libraries/maxminddb/*.php) IS tracked —
# only the .mmdb data file itself is excluded here.
*.mmdb

*.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

